[{"id": "96ee94ec3162", "text": "IS 456:2000 - Plain and Reinforced Concrete — Code of Practice (Fourth Revision). Foundational civil code covering design, structural safety, durability, mix proportions, reinforcement detailing, and minimum cementitious content for RCC works across India. Category: Building Materials. Status: Mandatory QCO. Clause Cl. 6.1.1: Characteristic Compressive Strength of Concrete. Compressive strength defined as that value of cube strength below which not more than 5 percent of test results fall. Standard grade designations range from M10 to M80 with 28-day 150mm cube curing. Clause Cl. 8.2.2.1: Durability & Minimum Cementitious Content (Table 5). For 'Severe' environmental exposure, minimum grade of reinforced concrete is M30; minimum cement content is 320 kg/m³ with maximum free water-cement ratio capped strictly at 0.45. Clause Cl. 26.5.1.1: Minimum and Maximum Tensile Reinforcement in Beams. Minimum longitudinal tension reinforcement ratio: As / (b * d) ≥ 0.85 / fy. Maximum reinforcement area in tension or compression shall not exceed 0.04 * b * D.", "embedding": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.21320071635561041, 0.053300179088902604, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.15990053726670783, 0.0, 0.0, 0.053300179088902604, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.053300179088902604, 0.053300179088902604, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.10660035817780521, 0.0, 0.0, -0.053300179088902604, 0.0, 0.21320071635561041, 0.053300179088902604, -0.053300179088902604, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.053300179088902604, 0.0, 0.10660035817780521, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.053300179088902604, 0.0, 0.0, 0.053300179088902604, 0.0, -0.053300179088902604, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.053300179088902604, 0.053300179088902604, 0.0, 0.0, 0.053300179088902604, 0.0, 0.0, -0.053300179088902604, 0.0, -0.10660035817780521, -0.31980107453341566, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.053300179088902604, 0.053300179088902604, 0.0, 0.0, -0.053300179088902604, 0.053300179088902604, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.10660035817780521, 0.0, -0.053300179088902604, 0.15990053726670783, -0.053300